<h1>Current MacBook Lineup</h1>
<p>
  The MacBook Pro 16″ and 14″ offer M5 Max and M5 Pro chips for demanding creative and development workloads. The 14″ now starts with the M6, a generation newer than the chips above it, with twice their Neural Engine cores and the same 24-hour battery life as the 16″ with M5 Pro. The MacBook Pro PROLED XDR Display models sit alongside them in both sizes, pairing the M5 Pro and M5 Max with a tandem OLED touchscreen. The MacBook Air 13″ and 15″ carry the base M5 — the best all-rounder for most people, with strong single-threaded performance and all-day battery life. The MacBook Neo slots in with an A18 Pro for ultra-portable use where weight matters more than sustained performance.
</p>

